Governor notes for the planner (16:33Z).

Scope: this row is ps1-only. On Windows PowerShell 5.1, `return ($text | ConvertFrom-Json)` in Invoke-MoeRpc (scripts/moe-agent.ps1, around :1830) unrolls a one-element JSON array into its element.

Make the scalar/object consumers shape-preserving. Note that -NoEnumerate is pwsh 7 only. Keep every existing list caller's behaviour unchanged, and audit each Invoke-MoeRpc caller to show it.

Then add the CQ-M07n1 row this ruling deferred (comment on task-65b3e023): a malformed `[{profile:'verified-local',ready:true,…}]` readiness reply takes the same route as the sh twin's malformed reply.

The DoD here is the worker's one-liner. So the plan's verification must name concrete checks:
- the new and changed postflight-vm-route.ps1 rows under Windows PowerShell 5.1 and pwsh 7;
- postflight.ps1 under 5.1;
- bash scripts/tests/parity-check.sh;
- the UTF-8 BOM is kept.

Placement, with no dependsOn edge since this is worktree mode: the CQ-M07n chain edits moe-agent.ps1. n1 (65b3e023, live) adds a gate function near Stop-MoeWorktreeSeat and one call in the pre-flight. Keep this row's hunks inside Invoke-MoeRpc and the callers it audits, and edit with the Edit tool (no temp+mv). Land it before CQ-M07n (62ec51f1) closes the ps1 VM route.
